{"availability":"available","full":"rancher/k3k","name":"k3k","description":"Kubernetes in Kubernetes","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":914,"forks":88,"created":"2023-01-18T19:48:14Z","updated":"2026-10-08T09:45:36Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rancher.github.io/k3k-product-docs","topics":[],"demo":"https://rancher.github.io/k3k-product-docs","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.617Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.617Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.617Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.454Z","stars":914,"forks":87},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.617Z","stars":914,"forks":88}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["K3k, Kubernetes in Kubernetes, is a tool that empowers you to create and manage isolated K3s clusters within your existing Kubernetes environment. It enables efficient multi-tenancy, streamlined experimentation, and robust resource isolation, minimizing infrastructure costs by allowing you to run multiple lightweight Kubernetes clusters on the same physical host. K3k offers both \"shared\" mode, optimizing resource utilization, and \"virtual\" mode, providing more isolation with dedicated K3s server and agent pods. This allows you to access a full Kubernetes experience without the overhead of…","K3k integrates seamlessly with Rancher for simplified management of your embedded clusters."],"features":["Resource Isolation: Ensure workload isolation and prevent resource contention between teams or applications. K3k allows you to define resource limits and quotas for each embedded cluster, guaranteeing that one team's…","Simplified Multi-Tenancy: Easily create dedicated Kubernetes environments for different users or projects, simplifying access control and management. Provide each team with their own isolated cluster, complete with its…","Optimized Resource Utilization (Shared Mode): Maximize your infrastructure investment by running multiple K3s clusters on the same physical host. K3k's shared mode allows you to efficiently share underlying resources,…","Stronger Isolation (Virtual Mode): For enhanced isolation, K3k's virtual mode provides dedicated K3s server and agent pods for each embedded cluster, so every cluster gets its own control plane, CNI, and nodes, without…","Rancher Integration: Simplify the management of your K3k clusters with Rancher. Leverage Rancher's intuitive UI and powerful features to monitor, manage, and scale your embedded clusters with ease."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rancher/k3k/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"963b4a32b5280e8492f16214da4ee6d9c3664bb3ea19161caf7c1b5ed5804b07","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.784Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.779Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"K3k, Kubernetes in Kubernetes, is a tool that empowers you to create and manage isolated K3s clusters within your existing Kubernetes environment. It enables efficient multi-tenancy, streamlined experimentation, and robust resource isolation, minimizing infrastructure costs by allowing you to run multiple lightweight Kubernetes clusters on the same physical host. K3k offers both \"shared\" mode, optimizing resource utilization, and \"virtual\" mode, providing more isolation with dedicated K3s server and agent pods. This allows you to access a full Kubernetes experience without the overhead of…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rancher/k3k/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"963b4a32b5280e8492f16214da4ee6d9c3664bb3ea19161caf7c1b5ed5804b07","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rancher/k3k/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.779Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T09:45:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rancher/k3k/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.780Z","hash":"963b4a32b5280e8492f16214da4ee6d9c3664bb3ea19161caf7c1b5ed5804b0